#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0898 expect=skipped domain=ADAE
#note "ASEQ, SRCSEQ and RECSEQ all match the &DOMSEQ pattern but are NOT parent references - ASEQ is ADaM own sequence and SRCSEQ names its parent in SRCDOM, not in the variable name. known_domain_only drops all three because A / SRC / REC are not library domains, so the rule is skipped rather than checking ASEQ against a dataset called A. The datasets A, SRC and REC below are loaded ON PURPOSE: without them the parent-not-loaded check would drop all three candidates anyway and this scenario would stay green with known_domain_only removed - i.e. it would pin nothing. The same masking made two unit tests vacuous before it was caught."
#library standard=adamig version=1-2
#library standard-domains AE CM MH DM LB VS
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col ASEQ    type=Char
col SRCSEQ  type=Char
col RECSEQ  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1 | 1 | 1
---

dataset A
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col ASEQ    type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1
---

dataset SRC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SRCSEQ  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1
---

dataset REC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col RECSEQ  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1
---
